  "semantics": {
    "definition": "The code every element of the new 3D world shares: what an element can be, held as data; its outline and the ground it covers; the one grid of studs; the strips bent into a Möbius loop or curled as a wave; the light; and three.js making an element from its data, with its surfaces, its states and its glow. Every number and colour it draws with is Eidos’s.",
    "responsibility": "Hold what several Eidos components share, once. It changes only through a proposal you approve; Mero keeps the fingerprints of the version you approved, git keeps the code."
